=== This package should contain the following files:

Makefile
	Type "make" for constructing the "MinimalAbsentWords" executable.

MinimalAbsentWords.c
	The main program.

int.h
	Defines the type INT as "long int". This should work both in 32 and
	in 64-bit architectures. In 32-bit architectures INT should be a
	32-bit integer whereas in 64-bit architectures it should be a 64-bit
	integer. At start up, the program prints the number of bits that it
	is using for INT.

	Note that when using 32-bit ints the size of the string as well as
	that of the suffix array are obviously limited to 2^32 - 1.

lcp.c lcp.h
	Functions for constructing the longest common prefix array by a
	linear time method due to Kasai et al.
	Original code from M. Douglas McIlroy's website
	http://www.cs.dartmouth.edu/~doug/sarray/ with some
	minor adaptations for complying with our needs.

sarray.c sarray.h
	Functions for constructing the suffix array.
	Original code from M. Douglas McIlroy's website
	http://www.cs.dartmouth.edu/~doug/sarray/ with some
	minor adaptations for complying with our needs.

stack.c stack.h
	Functions for handling stacks of lcp intervals.

example.fa
	Small example of a DNA sequence in fasta format. It includes two "N"
	letters, which are interpreted as string delimiters. Letters are
	interpreted in the following way:
		A,C,G,T,a,c,g,t - DNA (valid) letters
		newlines - ignored
		lines starting with ">" - ignored (fasta comments)
		all remaining letters - string delimiters

=== The program has the following interface:

MinimalAbsentWords maxSize
                   [ -m (less mem, but slower) ]
                   [ -w (write to stdout) ]
                   [ -rc (reversed complement) ]
                   [ -n len (write only words of size len) ]
                   file [ file ... ]

maxSize
	Maximum size of word that is searched.

-m
	Constructs the suffix array using qsort. This requires about half of
	the memory required by the default action, but it is (much) slower. Its
	main purpose is debugging.

-w
	By default, the program reports only the number of minimal absent words
	found. This option also lists all those words.

-rc
	Considers the reversed complement of the sequence.

-n len
	Write only the minimal absent words of size "len".

file [ file ... ]
	One or more sequence files in fasta or in gzip fasta format.

=== Examples

shell prompt> MinimalAbsentWords 10 -rc example.fa
using indexes with 32 bits
reading data... done: 0 s
got 19 valid DNA bases (i.e., ACGT or acgt)
building suffix array... done: 0 s
found 3 sub-string(s)
building lcp array... done: 0 s
searching minimal absent words... done: 0 s
found 26 minimal absent words of size 3
found 17 minimal absent words of size 4
found 2 minimal absent words of size 6
size of largest maximal repeat: 4
found a total of 45 minimal absent words
total time used: 0 s

shell prompt> MinimalAbsentWords 10 -n 6 -rc example.fa
using indexes with 32 bits
reading data... done: 0 s
got 19 valid DNA bases (i.e., ACGT or acgt)
building suffix array... done: 0 s
found 3 sub-string(s)
building lcp array... done: 0 s
searching minimal absent words... done: 0 s
found 26 minimal absent words of size 3
found 17 minimal absent words of size 4
found 2 minimal absent words of size 6
size of largest maximal repeat: 4
found a total of 45 minimal absent words
total time used: 0 s
